From 6c93675713f50ec9a1b2c5b23313cd500a3f3ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Coreader integration <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:37:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Index Coreader reading notes in place

Coreader keeps each book's highlights and notes in one Markdown file,
<library>/Books/<slug>/notes.md. Mirror those files the way the other
Personal OS mirrors work: record where each file is (relative to the
library) plus a search index rebuilt from the file, and let Ask read the
file itself. Nothing is copied into the vault and the library is never
written to.

The [coreader] table of config.toml is reread on every scan, so
`mastisk coreader connect` and `disconnect` take effect without a
daemon restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
